      "description": "Watch Levski Sofia vs Salzburg highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 17, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling European night as Levski Sofia welcomed Salzburg for a high-stakes encounter in the UEFA Europa League . With both teams eager to make their mark on the group stage, the atmosphere was thick with anticipation from the opening whistle. Tabaković Breaks the Deadlock On September 17, 2026, the match began as a tactical chess match, with both sides testing each other's defensive resolve. It was Salzburg who eventually found the breakthrough in the 39th minute. Haris Tabaković showcased his clinical instincts by finding the back of the net, silencing the home crowd and giving the visitors a crucial lead. The intensity of the match was evident shortly after, as Sota Kitano picked up the first booking of the evening just before the half-time whistle, signaling a feisty second half to come. A Battle of Attrition in the Second Half Following the restart, the game shifted into a more physical contest as Levski Sofia pushed for an equalizer. The referee remained busy, issuing a flurry of yellow cards to maintain control. Alex Centelles was cautioned for the hosts, while Haris Tabaković , Bartosz Mazurek , and Yorbe Vertessen all saw yellow for Salzburg during a heated middle period. Both managers looked to their benches to inject fresh energy; Damir Redzic and Karim Konate were introduced for the visitors, while Levski brought on Juan Perea and Mazire Soula to bolster their attacking options. Resilient Salzburg Closes it Out As the clock ticked toward full-time, the tension reached its peak. Levski Sofia made a double substitution in the 88th minute, bringing on Asen Mitkov and Stivan Stoyanchov for a final assault. However, Salzburg ’s defensive organization remained disciplined under pressure. Deep into stoppage time, Abubakr Barry received a yellow card as the visitors fought to protect their advantage. Ultimately, the referee's final whistle after four minutes of added time confirmed a hard-earned victory for Salzburg , secured by that pivotal first-half goal from Tabaković ."
